# {{ course_code }} — {{ course_name }}

This course repository was generated from the course Copier template. It keeps
course content here and uses the shared Python framework for publication,
student repositories, grading, and syllabus synchronization.

## Initial Setup

1. Review `course-config.yaml`, especially Canvas/Slack URLs and the first cohort.
2. Add student emails to `student_lists/students.{{ cohort_slug }}.txt`.
3. Replace the starter text in `syllabus.md.j2` with this course's syllabus.
4. Add assignments, labs, and demos in their corresponding directories.
5. Install the management tools with `uv sync --extra course-management`.

## Course Management

```bash
python scripts/manage_course.py --help
python scripts/manage_course.py publish-base --target {{ cohort_slug }}
python scripts/manage_course.py provision-student-repos --target {{ cohort_slug }}
```

`publish-base` creates or updates the safe cohort base. Students update their
own work with the generated `scripts/update_from_base.sh` script after a new
base release. See `scripts/management/README.md` for all commands.

## Updating the Framework

Copier records this course's template answers in `.copier-answers.yml`. Commit
that file. To apply a later template revision from a clean working tree:

```bash
copier update
```

Review and resolve any conflicts before committing the update.

## Docker Images

Build an image from `docker/Dockerfile` with an explicit registry tag:

```bash
./scripts/build_docker.sh --image ghcr.io/OWNER/{{ course_code | lower }}:latest
```

The helper supports ordinary Dockerfiles by default. For a multi-stage
Dockerfile, add `--target <stage>`. To test one platform locally without
pushing, use `--platforms linux/arm64 --no-push --load` (choose the platform
for your machine).
